* Models for the field-input simulations (Hall encoder and limit/E-stop
* inputs on the Robo sheet). Behavioural, fitted to datasheet numbers.

.options method=gear rshunt=1e9

* D16-D20, D22 TPESD0402G12V: bidirectional polymer ESD suppressor. It is
* open (0.05 pF) until about 450 V, then snaps back and clamps near 40 V
* (datasheet, 8 kV contact). Modelled as two switches with hysteresis (on
* above 450 V, off below 30 V), each with a 40 V, 1 ohm clamp.
.subckt POLYESD A K
C0 A K 0.05p
S1 A n1 A K SPOLY
Vcl1 n1 n2 40
Rcl1 n2 n3 1
D1 n3 K DPOLY
S2 K m1 K A SPOLY
Vcl2 m1 m2 40
Rcl2 m2 m3 1
D2 m3 A DPOLY
.model SPOLY SW(Ron=0.1 Roff=1e12 Vt=240 Vh=210)
.model DPOLY D(Is=1e-12)
.ends

* Alternative for comparison (not on the board): a 5 V unidirectional TVS
* diode such as an SMF5.0A-class part, VBR about 6.4 V, about 0.5 ohm
* dynamic resistance (about 14 V at 15 A).
.subckt TVS5V A K
* single diode: anode on ground (K), cathode on the line (A)
D1 K A DTVS
.model DTVS D(Is=1e-12 N=1.3 Rs=0.5 BV=6.4 IBV=1m Cjo=200p)
.ends

* RoboClaw input pin: 3.3 V CMOS logic, 5 V tolerant ("internal current
* limiting and voltage clipping", manual). Modelled as 10 pF with clamp
* diodes to 0 V and 5.5 V; the clamp current is reported.
.subckt RCPIN P
Cin P 0 10p
Dhi P vcl DCLP
Vcl vcl 0 5.5
Dlo nlo P DCLP
Vlo nlo 0 0
.model DCLP D(Is=1e-14 N=1.2 Rs=2)
.ends

* Open-collector Hall output (or a switch contact): closes when ctl > 0.5
.model SOC SW(Ron=20 Roff=1e9 Vt=0.5 Vh=0.05)

* Cable: one 0.5 m section of a wire in a multi-core cable
* (about 0.1 ohm/m, 0.6 uH/m, 60 pF/m to the other wires/ground)
.subckt CABSEG A B
R1 A n1 0.05
L1 n1 B 0.3u
C1 B 0 30p
.ends
